BOOT PROCESS:
BIOS AND UEFI - SAME AS WINDOWS


MBR (MASTER BOOT RECORD): #PART OF THE 1ST STAGE BOOTLOADER#
    |--> contains information on partitions locations on the hard drive. Partitions contain the 2nd stage bootloader known as the GRUB(Grand Unified Bootloader).
          (BOOTSTRAP): initial section of code that contains a bootloader known as GRUB broken into two stages
                        |--> 1ST STAGE- GRUB 1 --> LOADS GRUB 2 FROM SELECTED ACTIVE PARTITION 

MBR (MASTER BOOT RECORD) LAYOUT :
    |--> Address 	          Description 	                    Size (bytes)
        0x0000 (0)          BOOTSTARP CODE AREA                     446     
        0x01BE (446)        Partition Entry #1                       16   <---------------|
        0x01CE (462)        Partition Entry #2                       16                   |----(PARTITION TABLE) BROKEN INTO 4 SECTORS 
        0x01DE (478)        Partition Entry #3                       16                   |
        0x01EE (494)        Partition Entry #4                       16   <---------------|
        0x01FF (510)         0x55    BOOT SIGNATURE                   2   
	                                                              TOTAL= 512 BYTES


GUID PARTITION TABLE(GPT): #PART OF THE FIRST STAGE BOOTLOADER#
    |--> NEW VERSION OF THE MBR, DOES THE EXACT SAME THING 
          |--> ONLY WORKS WITH UEFI 
                HAS MANY BOOT SECTORS FOR REDUNDANCY 
                SUPPORTS 128 SEPERATE PHYSICAL PARTITIONS, MBR ONLY HAS 4
                SUPPORTS PARTITIONS UP TO 9 ZETTBYTES


