INIT (INITIALIZATION):
    |--> 7 DIFFERENT MODE FOR COMPUTER INTERACTION WITH THE USER
Run Level 	                    Meaning 	                                                          Description
0                                Halt                                                                Shutdown the system
1                                Single User                                                         single user to login, No network functionality, Used to troubleshoot.
2                                Multi-user mode                                                     multiple user to login, No network functionality
3                                Multi-user mode with networking                                     multiple user to login, all networking functionality
4                                Not used/user-definable                                             can be set to anything
5                                Multi-user mode with networking and GUI Desktop                     multiple user to login, all networking functionality, graphical desktop instead of a Bash terminal
6                                Reboot                                                              Restart the system


